  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div> <p>From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</p> </div><div lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" id=\"mw-content-text\">\n\n<table>\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_sp_(19797152176).jpg\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg/250px-Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"322\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg/500px-Costasiella_sp_%2819797152176%29.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"1536\" data-file-height=\"1977\"></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakatobi_National_Park\" title=\"Wakatobi National Park\">Wakatobi National Park</a>, 2015\n</td></tr> <tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxonomy_(biology)\" title=\"Taxonomy (biology)\">Scientific classification</a> <span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Taxonomy/Costasiella\" title=\"Edit this classification\"><img alt=\"Edit this classification\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_edit-ltr.svg.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"20\" data-file-height=\"20\"></a></span></span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kingdom:\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal\" title=\"Animal\">Animalia</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Phylum:\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mollusca\" title=\"Mollusca\">Mollusca</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Class:\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastropoda\" title=\"Gastropoda\">Gastropoda</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Family:\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costasiellidae\" title=\"Costasiellidae\">Costasiellidae</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Genus:\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costasiella\" title=\"Costasiella\"><i>Costasiella</i></a>\n</td></tr> <tr>\n<td>Species:\n</td>\n<td><p><i><b>C.&nbsp;kuroshimae</b></i></p>\n</td></tr> <tr>\n<th colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binomial_nomenclature\" title=\"Binomial nomenclature\">Binomial name</a>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"><b><span><span></span><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i></span></b><p>Ichikawa, 1993</p>\n</td></tr> <tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png/250px-Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"215\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png/500px-Costasiella-kuroshimae-distribution.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"763\" data-file-height=\"655\"></a></span>\n</td></tr> </tbody></table>\n<p><i><b>Costasiella kuroshimae</b></i> (also known as a <b>leaf slug</b>, <b>sea sheep</b>, or <b>leaf sheep</b>) is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Species\" title=\"Species\">species</a> of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sacoglossa\" title=\"Sacoglossa\">sacoglossan</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_slug\" title=\"Sea slug\">sea slug</a>. <i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> are shell-less <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean\" title=\"Ocean\">marine</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opisthobranch\" title=\"Opisthobranch\">opisthobranch</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastropod\" title=\"Gastropod\">gastropod</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mollusk\" title=\"Mollusk\">mollusks</a> in the family <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costasiellidae\" title=\"Costasiellidae\">Costasiellidae</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-WoRMS_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-WoRMS-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup> Despite being animals, they perform <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photosynthesis\" title=\"Photosynthesis\">photosynthesis</a>, via <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleptoplasty\" title=\"Kleptoplasty\">kleptoplasty</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span>[</span>2<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\">\n\n<p>Discovered in 1993 off the coast of the Japanese island <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuroshima_(Okinawa)\" title=\"Kuroshima (Okinawa)\">Kuroshima</a>, <i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> have been found in the waters near Japan, the Philippines, and Indonesia. They live in tropical climates.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span>[</span>3<span>]</span></a></sup> The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_locality_(biology)\" title=\"Type locality (biology)\">type locality</a> is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuroshima,_Taketomi,_Okinawa\" title=\"Kuroshima, Taketomi, Okinawa\">Kuroshima, Taketomi, Okinawa</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryukyu_Islands\" title=\"Ryukyu Islands\">Ryukyu Islands</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Jensen_2007_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Jensen_2007-4\"><span>[</span>4<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>They have two dark eyes and two <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinophore\" title=\"Rhinophore\">rhinophores</a> that emerge from the tops of their heads that look similar to sheep's ears or insect <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antenna_(biology)\" title=\"Antenna (biology)\">antennae</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Oceana_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Oceana-5\"><span>[</span>5<span>]</span></a></sup> They range in size from 5 to 10&nbsp;mm (<span><span>1</span>⁄<span>4</span></span> to <span><span>3</span>⁄<span>8</span></span> inch) in length. Their leaf-like appearance is credited to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerata\" title=\"Cerata\">cerata</a> featured in rows across their body. These cerata contain digestive glands that assist the <i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> in obtaining and storing food. They also aid in defense and respiration. <sup id=\"cite_ref-6\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span>[</span>6<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> are capable of a physiological process called kleptoplasty, in which they retain the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloroplast\" title=\"Chloroplast\">chloroplasts</a> from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algae\" title=\"Algae\">algae</a> they feed on. Absorbing the chloroplasts from algae enables them to perform photosynthesis.<sup id=\"cite_ref-7\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span>[</span>7<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> is a selective feeder of algae from the genus <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avrainvillea\" title=\"Avrainvillea\">Avrainvillea</a></i>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-Oceana_5-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Oceana-5\"><span>[</span>5<span>]</span></a></sup> from which it sequesters chloroplasts into its own cells, retaining them for short-term photosynthesis. Even in the absence of active photosynthesis, chloroplasts provide a nutrient storage or \"larder\" that facilitates the survival of the slug without food for an extended period of time.<sup id=\"cite_ref-8\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span>[</span>8<span>]</span></a></sup> This points out the peculiar adaptation of <i>C. kuroshimae</i> among nonphotosynthetic marine animals.\n</p>\n\n<ul> <li> <p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_Kuroshimae_(19080120525)_(2).jpg\" title=\"A frontal picture of a Costasiella kuroshimae.\"><img alt=\"A frontal picture of a Costasiella kuroshimae.\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg/120px-Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"85\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg/250px-Costasiella_Kuroshimae_%2819080120525%29_%282%29.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"2900\" data-file-height=\"2058\"></a></span></p> <p>A frontal picture of a <i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i>.</p> </li> <li> <p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_kuroshimae_taken_in_Anilao_Philippines.png\" title=\"Costasiella kuroshimae taken in Secret Bay Anilao dive site, Batangas, Philippines\"><img alt=\"Costasiella kuroshimae taken in Secret Bay Anilao dive site, Batangas, Philippines\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Costasiella_kuroshimae_taken_in_Anilao_Philippines.png/120px-Costasiella_kuroshimae_taken_in_Anilao_Philippines.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"84\" height=\"120\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Costasiella_kuroshimae_taken_in_Anilao_Philippines.png/250px-Costasiella_kuroshimae_taken_in_Anilao_Philippines.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"396\" data-file-height=\"565\"></a></span></p> <p><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> taken in Secret Bay Anilao dive site, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batangas\" title=\"Batangas\">Batangas</a>, Philippines</p> </li> <li> <p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_kuroshimae,_Koh_Phangan.jpg\" title=\"Costasiella kuroshimae at Koh Phangan, 2014\"><img alt=\"Costasiella kuroshimae at Koh Phangan, 2014\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Costasiella_kuroshimae%2C_Koh_Phangan.jpg/120px-Costasiella_kuroshimae%2C_Koh_Phangan.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"103\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Costasiella_kuroshimae%2C_Koh_Phangan.jpg/250px-Costasiella_kuroshimae%2C_Koh_Phangan.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"768\" data-file-height=\"659\"></a></span></p> <div><p><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koh_Phangan\" title=\"Koh Phangan\">Koh Phangan</a>, 2014</p></div> </li> <li> <p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_y_puesta.jpg\" title=\"Costasiella kuroshimae at Bali, Indonesia.\"><img alt=\"Costasiella kuroshimae at Bali, Indonesia.\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Costasiella_y_puesta.jpg/120px-Costasiella_y_puesta.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"90\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Costasiella_y_puesta.jpg/250px-Costasiella_y_puesta.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"1235\" data-file-height=\"928\"></a></span></p> <p><i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> at Bali, Indonesia.</p> </li> <li> <p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Costasiella_cf_kuroshimae.png\" title=\"Costasiella cf. kuroshimae on Avrainvillea erecta. Locality: Lizard Island, Great Barrier Reef. The length of the slug is about 1&nbsp;cm (3⁄8&nbsp;in).\"><img alt=\"Costasiella cf. kuroshimae on Avrainvillea erecta. Locality: Lizard Island, Great Barrier Reef. The length of the slug is about 1&nbsp;cm (3⁄8&nbsp;in).\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Costasiella_cf_kuroshimae.png/120px-Costasiella_cf_kuroshimae.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"80\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Costasiella_cf_kuroshimae.png/250px-Costasiella_cf_kuroshimae.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"324\" data-file-height=\"217\"></a></span></p> <div><p><i>Costasiella</i> cf. <i>kuroshimae</i> on <i>Avrainvillea erecta</i>. Locality: Lizard Island, Great Barrier Reef. The length of the slug is about </p><p>1&nbsp;cm (<span><span>3</span>⁄<span>8</span></span>&nbsp;in).</p></div> </li>\n</ul>\n\n<div><ol>\n<li id=\"cite_note-WoRMS-1\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-WoRMS_1-0\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFBouchet2014\">Bouchet P (2014). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.marinespecies.org/aphia.php?p=taxdetails&amp;id=494655\">\"<i>Costasiella kuroshimae</i> Ichikawa 1993\"</a>. <i>World Register of Marine Species</i><span>. Retrieved <span>17 January</span> 2015</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=World+Register+of+Marine+Species&amp;rft.atitle=Costasiella+kuroshimae+Ichikawa+1993&amp;rft.date=2014&amp;rft.aulast=Bouchet&amp;rft.aufirst=P&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.marinespecies.org%2Faphia.php%3Fp%3Dtaxdetails%26id%3D494655&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ACostasiella+kuroshimae\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFChristaB._GouldFrankenVleugels2014\">Christa, Gregor; B. Gould, Sven; Franken, Johanna; Vleugels, Manja; Karmeinski, Dario; Handeler, Katharina; F. Martin, William; Wagele, Heike (23 May 2014). \"Functional kleptoplasty in a limapontioidean genus: phylogeny, food preferences and photosynthesis in Costasiella, with a focus on C. ocellifera (Gastropoda: Sacoglossa)\". <i>Journal of Molluscan Studies</i>. <b>80</b> (5): <span>499–</span>507. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1093%2Fmollus%2Feyu026\">10.1093/mollus/eyu026</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Journal+of+Molluscan+Studies&amp;rft.atitle=Functional+kleptoplasty+in+a+limapontioidean+genus%3A+phylogeny%2C+food+preferences+and+photosynthesis+in+Costasiella%2C+with+a+focus+on+C.+ocellifera+%28Gastropoda%3A+